About the Demo
--------------

This demo made the second place at the demo competition of THE PARTY 3 in
Herning / Denmark.

This demo is designed to work also on not-so-powerfull computers. In fact
I've tested it on a 286 and it worked fine.
There are some rumors, that there are some bugs on a 486-66 with a local bus
ET-4000.... Hmm. strange. But hey, just let it run on a slower computer ;-)

The demo needs 600.000 Bytes of free conventional Memory. No EMS is needed.
In fact, the demo won't run with an EMS-driver.

The demo uses exclusively the Gravis Ultrasound for music output. A 256k GUS
will do.


Release Fuck-Ups
----------------

Well, it's no secret, that the so-called 'Amiga-organizers' kinda fucked up
parts of the pc-part of the party. Their Masterpiece was to force all atten-
dants of the demo competition to release their demos, even if they were not
finished. Well. I know that the Demo of Stone/Dust isn't finished yet, my
demo was only finished 95%, and the demo by Infiny wasn't absolutely ready
either!

So the top 3 demos weren't finished, but still they wanted them released.
I talked to Lord Cyrix / Access Denied, and he told me that I've got time
till the 10th of January to finish everything, so that sounded o.k. to me!

But today (which is the 7th of January, the day I actually finished the demo)
I learned that the demo-fragments where released allready. Hmm.

Well. THIS is the final version of GBU, so it's not my fault you had to down-
load it twice.

